CAT = "nzreTenure"; SEG = "TEN"
Q = [
("A buyer's lawyer runs a title search. Besides the owner's name, what may it show?",
 "Caveats and easements", ["The buyer's credit rating", "The vendor's tax return", "The agent's commission"],
 "REA's guide says a title search checks who the legal owner is and any other interests over the property, such as caveats or easements."),
("Under the Property Law Act 2007, what covenant is implied into every lease about rent?",
 "The lessee must pay rent when due", ["The lessor pays the rates as rent", "Rent is paid only at the end", "Rent is optional in year one"],
 "REA material says section 218 and Schedule 3 imply into all leases that the lessee must pay the rent when it is due under the lease."),
("A tenant under a commercial lease wants to alter the premises. What does the implied covenant say?",
 "The lessor's consent is needed", ["Alterations are always allowed", "Alterations need council approval only", "Alterations need the agent's approval"],
 "REA material lists the implied covenant that the lessee will not carry out alterations without the lessor's consent."),
("Which right does the lessor have under the implied lease terms?",
 "To inspect at reasonable times", ["To enter at any hour unannounced", "To live in part of the premises", "To change the rent each month"],
 "The implied terms entitle the lessor to enter the premises at all reasonable times to view their state of repair."),
("Rent under a lease has been in arrears for 15 working days. What may the lessor do under the implied terms?",
 "Re-enter the premises", ["Cancel the title", "Sell the lessee's goods at once", "Sue the agent for the debt"],
 "The implied terms let the lessor re-enter peaceably if rent, or part of it, is in arrears for 15 working days. Re-entry does not relieve the lessee of liability."),
("What does the implied covenant of quiet enjoyment give a lessee?",
 "Peaceful use of the premises", ["Free rent during quiet periods", "A right to sublet to anybody", "A right to change the locks"],
 "REA material lists quiet enjoyment of the premises as a lessee's implied right under the Property Law Act 2007."),
("A lease says the lessee needs the lessor's consent before assigning. Under section 224 the lessor:",
 "Must not unreasonably refuse", ["May refuse for any reason at all", "Must always say yes to it", "Must reply in writing next day"],
 "Where consent is required as a term of a lease, section 224 says it must not be unreasonably withheld."),
("What is an Agreement to Lease (Heads of Agreement)?",
 "A promise to grant a lease", ["The final lease deed itself", "A sale agreement for the land", "A bond receipt for tenants"],
 "REA material says it is an agreement to grant a lease in the future, usually the first document negotiated, while the Deed of Lease records the actual grant."),
("In a commercial leasing transaction, who is usually the agency's client?",
 "The lessor", ["The lessee", "The council", "The lessee's bank"],
 "REA material says the lessee is usually the third party (customer) and the agency relationship is in most situations between the agent and the lessor, the client."),
("A licensee lists a house with sitting tenants. Which two matters should the licensee consider?",
 "Viewing access and notice", ["Insulation ratings and the bond", "Commission and school zones", "Rates and mortgage terms"],
 "REA's note on the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 says that when listing a tenanted residential property, licensees should consider access rights for viewings and notice periods for ending a tenancy."),
("A licensee markets a unit title apartment. What must the licensee understand so marketing is accurate?",
 "Body corporate rules and papers", ["The neighbour's mortgage terms", "The tenants' bond lodgement details", "The developer's profit margin"],
 "REA material says licensees marketing unit title properties must understand the body corporate rules and other documents that form part of the required disclosure."),
("Which of these is a \"transaction\" under the Real Estate Agents Act?",
 "A village occupation right sale", ["The hire of a holiday camper car", "A sale of household furniture", "The lending of money on mortgage"],
 "Section 4 includes the grant, sale or other disposal of an occupation right agreement under the Retirement Villages Act 2003 as a transaction."),
]
